                // its own short argument. However, if any of the arguments
                // takes a value, then the *rest* of the string is used as
                // its value, and if there’s no rest of the string, then it
                // uses the next one in the iterator.
                //
                //   -a        => ‘a’
                //   -abc      => ‘a’, ‘b’, ‘c’
                //   -abxdef   => ‘a’, ‘b’, ‘x=def’
                //   -abx def  => ‘a’, ‘b’, ‘x=def’
                //   -abx      =>  error
